# 27. Rule Adjustments

If testing reveals a rule that cannot be implemented reliably as currently written:

1. do not hide the problem in validator code
2. document the ambiguity
3. determine whether the rule needs clarification
4. update the rule inventory/classification if required
5. update the implementation specification
6. add a regression test

Rule changes should remain traceable to the original rule ID.

---

# 28. Success Criteria

CP-AUTO-009 should not define success as:

```text
Zero findings.
```

A repository may legitimately contain content issues.

Instead, success means:

- findings are explainable
- true violations are detected
- valid structures are not incorrectly rejected
- Foundation and OT differences are handled correctly
- rule severity is respected
- output is trustworthy
- known edge cases have regression tests
- remaining semantic questions are correctly deferred

---

# 29. Acceptance Criteria

CP-AUTO-009 is complete when:

- [ ] All six Foundation modules have been tested.
- [ ] Both OT modules have been tested.
- [ ] All four validators have been exercised.
- [ ] A baseline machine-readable QA result has been captured.
- [ ] Every baseline finding has been reviewed.
- [ ] False positives have been identified and resolved or documented.
- [ ] False negatives have been tested with controlled fixtures.
- [ ] Foundation/OT structural differences have been verified.
- [ ] Frontmatter behavior has been calibrated against live content.
- [ ] Style detection has been verified against actual source.
- [ ] Scenario/company matching has been verified.
- [ ] Cabinet/lab relationships have been verified.
- [ ] Cascading findings have been reviewed.
- [ ] File/line/column reporting has been checked.
- [ ] Output conforms to CP-AUTO-004.
- [ ] Exit codes conform to CP-AUTO-004.
- [ ] Regression tests exist for discovered validator bugs.
- [ ] No production content was changed merely to satisfy an incorrect validator.
- [ ] No AI is required for deterministic QA.
- [ ] Remaining semantic questions are explicitly deferred to later review.

---

# 30. Definition of Done

CP-AUTO-009 is successful when the CyberPivot team can trust the deterministic QA engine enough to run it on a pull request without treating the validator itself as an uncontrolled source of noise.

The key question is:

> "If this QA engine flags something, can I understand why it flagged it and trust that the rule actually applies?"

Only when the answer is yes should the system move to GitHub integration.

